1214	// ==========================================================================
1215	// T1 REWORK7-A — the structural registration admission budget and the
1216	// route-specific registration mail-permit deadline.
1217	//
1218	// Two earlier claims are repaired here.
1219	//
1220	// The first is what "103" means. decision_version 2 published it as a MEASURED
1221	// accepted-request capacity, and unchanged-code RED evidence then contradicted
1222	// that: the same burst accepted 98, then 96. 103 is now what it structurally
1223	// is — a process-owned admission budget with no wait queue, taken synchronously
1224	// before the first repository await, so the 104th valid request is refused
1225	// before any repository, limiter, KDF, mail, token or mutation work happens.
1226	//
1227	// The second is the wait deadline. Three fresh diagnostic processes committed
1228	// and sent all 103 registrations with zero refusals once the registration wait
1229	// ceiling was widened, at a worst reservation wait of 21,902.2 ms. The shipped
1230	// 18,000 ms bound was therefore censoring real admissions rather than bounding
1231	// lost capacity. Registration alone now waits 28,000 ms; resend keeps 18,000.
1232	//
1233	// Every lifecycle assertion below is driven by an explicit barrier, a held
1234	// permit, or a test-local deadline. Nothing here sleeps for 28 seconds of wall
1235	// time, and the two tests that assert the EXACT ruled deadlines read them off
1236	// the unmodified production policy.
1237	// ==========================================================================
1238	
